// Status per those docs: drafted, NOT yet individually approved -- review before treating as final.
// Only the "Website copy (EN)" paragraphs are included here; internal source/review notes are excluded.
export const vehicleCopy: Record<string, string[]> = {
  "albany-alpha": ["The Albany Alpha keeps its tailoring sharp. This two-door sports coupe in GTA VI draws on Cadillac design, particularly the ATS, with the long hood and angular bodywork of a larger luxury car. It has enough presence for an expensive hotel entrance without looking like it arrived with a security detail.", "Inside, there’s room for two, with power going to the rear wheels. The Alpha’s appeal lies in its proportions and restrained styling: a proper coupe shape with a little American excess around the edges. Some cars need a bright paint job to get noticed. This one can keep its jacket on."],
  "albany-buccaneer": ["Long, broad and comfortably old-school, the Albany Buccaneer ’65 is an American coupe with presence in GTA VI. Its design blends Ford Fairlane and Buick Riviera influences, with a long body and a roofline that gives the whole car a relaxed, substantial presence. This is the standard Buccaneer, with the underlying shape doing most of the work.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout straightforward. There’s something appealing about a classic that looks complete before anyone starts planning a build. Park it alongside newer muscle and the difference is clear: the Buccaneer carries its age in the proportions, with the sort of confidence that doesn’t need a launch-control button."],
  "albany-cavalcade-xl": ["There is nothing discreet about the Albany Cavalcade XL in GTA VI. Cadillac Escalade-V-inspired styling sets the tone. Its upright front, long SUV body and commanding proportions leave little doubt about the brief: American luxury with plenty of visual weight. Subtle arrival plans may need revising.", "With four seats and all-wheel drive, the Cavalcade XL pairs its imposing outline with a familiar SUV layout. It belongs to the modern end of Albany’s range, where crisp detailing replaces the chrome-heavy elegance of the older cars. For a night out with the crew, it has the right presence before anyone has even opened a door."],
  "albany-emperor": ["The Albany Emperor ’85 wears its Cadillac ancestry openly. In GTA VI, this traditional American sedan draws on the late-1970s Sedan de Ville and the later Cadillac Brougham, bringing upright lines, generous proportions and a distinctly old-school sense of occasion.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive suit the familiar layout beneath that formal body. The Emperor’s character comes from an era when a luxury car announced itself with length and chrome rather than a screen across the dashboard. It looks equally convincing outside a neighborhood diner or at the end of a very long driveway. The appointment can wait; the entrance deserves a moment."],
  "albany-manana": ["Soft lines and generous proportions define the Albany Manana ’77, a classic American car in GTA VI. Buick LeSabre and Cadillac Eldorado influences give it a long, low shape, with the broad surfaces and decorative details that make older cruisers so easy to recognize.", "This two-seat, rear-wheel-drive Albany has a different appeal from the sharply styled sports cars around it. Its character is in the silhouette and the easygoing image, the kind of car you take out because the evening is still warm and there’s no good reason to head home yet. A little chrome can do more than a lot of carbon fiber."],
  "albany-primo": ["The Albany Primo is GTA VI’s kind of everyday American sedan: boxy, familiar and built around a shape you could lose in a supermarket parking lot. Its late-1980s Pontiac Bonneville influence shows in the straight body lines and conventional four-door proportions.", "With four seats and rear-wheel drive, the Primo keeps things simple. Its understated appearance is a large part of the appeal, especially in a garage full of cars trying very hard to look important. There’s room for an ordinary-looking sedan with a little character. The Primo looks like it has errands to run, even when its owner absolutely doesn’t."],
  "albany-v-str": ["The Albany V-STR gives GTA VI a sharp-edged American sports sedan with a clear Cadillac CTS-V influence. Its formal four-door profile meets more assertive styling at the nose, creating a car that looks comfortable outside an office but slightly impatient with the meeting.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive preserve the traditional sports-sedan layout. Visually, the V-STR sits well apart from Albany’s older cruisers: tighter lines, a lower-looking stance and a more modern attitude. It’s an appealing choice for anyone who likes their cars to look dressed for business without removing every trace of personality. The suit fits; the expression is less cooperative."],
  "annis-elegy-retro-custom": ["Nissan Skyline fans will find plenty to recognize in GTA VI’s Annis Elegy ’90. Its Nissan Skyline GT-R roots span three generations: an R32-inspired silhouette, an R33-style front end and details drawn from the R34. The result has its own identity while keeping the family resemblance easy to spot. GTA Online called it the Elegy Retro Custom.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive sit beneath that squared-off body. The Elegy’s appeal goes beyond a badge or a single styling cue: it captures the look of an era that still fills car-meet parking lots. If your taste runs to Japanese coupes from the ’90s, the introduction is probably unnecessary."],
  "annis-hellion": ["The Annis Hellion ’95 brings old-school 4x4 shape to GTA VI. Its square body and upright cabin are led by the fourth-generation Nissan Patrol Y60, with details that also recall the Nissan D21 and Jeep Cherokee XJ. Nothing about it looks delicate, and that is very much the point.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive give the Hellion a simple, purposeful layout. It has the kind of silhouette that looks better with dust on the body and somewhere unpaved in the background. For players who prefer straight edges, chunky tires and a little distance from the city, this Annis already understands the plan."],
  "benefactor-dubsta": ["The Benefactor Dubsta takes the Mercedes-Benz G-Class formula into GTA VI: a tall, square body with an unmistakably upright stance. Flat panels and a straight roofline give it an identity that survives every change in fashion around it. Curves were apparently someone else’s department.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive complete the familiar SUV layout. The Dubsta’s character comes from the contrast between its utilitarian shape and luxury-car presence. It can set the mood for a trip away from the city or look entirely at ease outside a high-end venue. Either way, you won’t mistake the outline for a rounded family crossover."],
  "benefactor-schafter-v12": ["The Benefactor Schafter V12 gives GTA VI the look of a German executive sedan with a less restrained side. Its Brabus E V12 inspiration explains the combination: familiar business-car proportions with a more purposeful attitude than the office parking lot strictly requires.", "The four-seat, rear-wheel-drive layout keeps the profile practical without making the car feel visually anonymous. This is a sedan for players who appreciate a long hood, a proper trunk and relatively discreet styling. A dark finish suits the mood, but the appeal is already in the shape. It looks like a promotion, followed by a questionable use of the bonus."],
  "benefactor-xls": ["With Mercedes-Benz GL-Class proportions and BMW X5 influences, the Benefactor XLS takes a familiar approach to the luxury SUV in GTA VI. A tall cabin and substantial body give it presence, with a more rounded appearance than Benefactor’s square-edged Dubsta.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive give the XLS a familiar foundation. Its appeal is less about making an entrance and more about looking comfortably established wherever it stops. For a garage built around understated modern cars, it fills the SUV slot without demanding a separate personality. Think weekend luggage, a decent hotel and someone insisting they know a better route."],
  "bravado-banshee": ["The Bravado Banshee is all long hood, low cabin and American sports-car attitude. Its Dodge Viper influence gives GTA VI a shape that looks dramatic without relying on a maze of sharp edges. The proportions make the introduction long before the badge does.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the Banshee focused on the classic sports-car formula. There’s little visual compromise in a body that devotes so much space to the nose and so little to passengers. It’s a car for players who want something bold and recognizable in the garage, with enough roadster-era swagger to make an ordinary parking space feel like a display stand."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "bravado-buffalo": ["The Bravado Buffalo ’07 puts Dodge Charger-inspired American muscle into a four-door shape in GTA VI. Its broad body and assertive front end give it more attitude than an ordinary commuter sedan, while the conventional roofline keeps the design grounded in something familiar.", "This is the Buffalo ’07 rather than the newer Buffalo ’19, and its simpler styling is part of the attraction. It looks like a car that could handle the weekday routine, provided nobody asks too many questions about why the driver is dressed for a car meet."],
  "bravado-buffalo-stx": ["A four-door body does little to soften the muscle-car image of the Bravado Buffalo ’19 in GTA VI. Its design takes cues from the 2015-era Dodge Charger. The shape is more contemporary than the Buffalo ’07, but the appeal is familiar: plenty of visual attitude, plus four doors. This is the generation GTA Online players know as the Buffalo STX.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive keep the Buffalo ’19 rooted in that American sports-sedan tradition. Its body has enough presence to hold its own among coupes without pretending the rear doors are an embarrassment. For a crew that likes muscle-car styling but travels together, the Buffalo ’19 makes a convincing entrance. Everyone gets a door; subtlety gets left outside."],
  "bravado-dorado": ["The Bravado Dorado takes its cues from the first-generation Dodge Durango, bringing a recognizable slice of turn-of-the-millennium SUV design to GTA VI. The tall body, rounded nose and sturdy-looking proportions have a different character from today’s sharply creased luxury crossovers.", "With four seats and all-wheel drive, the Dorado keeps the familiar family-SUV arrangement. Its styling has an everyday quality that works well in a garage with older pickups and American sedans. There’s a certain appeal to a vehicle that looks ready for a weekend away without also looking ready for a fashion campaign. Bring the cooler; the attitude is already included."],
  "bravado-gauntlet-classic": ["The Bravado Gauntlet Custom ’69 wears its first-generation Dodge Challenger inspiration proudly. In GTA VI, the long hood, short rear deck and broad coupe body capture the proportions that made early American pony cars so distinctive. There’s no need to explain the appeal of that silhouette to a muscle-car fan.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout true to the car’s character. The Classic is about the older end of the Gauntlet family, with simpler surfaces and a more period feel than the Hellfire. It’s the sort of car that turns a casual meet into a discussion about everybody’s dream garage."],
  "bravado-gauntlet-hellfire": ["The Bravado Gauntlet Hellfire takes the 2018 Dodge Challenger SRT Demon as a major design influence and brings that swollen, modern muscle-car look to GTA VI. Its broad body and confrontational front end give the Hellfire a very different presence from the older Gauntlet Custom ’69.", "This rear-wheel-drive two-seater makes its point through scale and shape. The cabin sits behind a substantial hood, and the whole car looks like it takes up more of the conversation than strictly necessary. For players drawn to contemporary American muscle, that’s part of the attraction. It has the visual manners of someone arriving late and parking at the front."],
  // buckingham-*: Codex Buckingham-Rebrand-Texte-2026-10-18.md (Fausto 18.10.: Jubilee + Windsor + Windsor Drop are Buckingham).
  "buckingham-jubilee": ["The Buckingham Jubilee makes a substantial entrance in GTA VI. This upright luxury SUV takes its styling cues from the Rolls-Royce Cullinan. Its formal proportions and imposing nose give it the air of a car that expects someone else to deal with the parking.", "Known as the Enus Jubilee in GTA Online, it returns with Buckingham branding in GTA VI. Four seats and all-wheel drive provide the familiar SUV layout beneath the grand presentation. The Jubilee’s appeal is about presence: less sports-car theater, more private-entrance confidence. It suits a polished collection where the everyday vehicle is allowed to look just as expensive as the weekend one. Even a quick trip across town can have the atmosphere of a reservation made under somebody important’s name."],
  "buckingham-windsor-drop": ["Roof down, long hood out front, four seats behind that formal nose: the Buckingham Windsor Drop gives the luxury coupe idea a different outlook. Its Rolls-Royce Dawn inspiration comes through in the generous bodywork and open cabin. This is a convertible that makes room for the whole crew without giving up the occasion.", "Seen in GTA VI’s Launch Trailer, the car returns under Buckingham after appearing in GTA Online as the Enus Windsor Drop. Rear-wheel drive sits beneath the grand presentation. The Drop leaves the roof out of the conversation. Bring sunglasses; the rear passengers will want theirs too."],
  "canis-mesa": ["Upright, compact and rugged-looking, the Canis Mesa is GTA VI’s take on the Jeep Wrangler-inspired SUV. The near-vertical front and compact SUV proportions make its identity clear without relying on elaborate trim or oversized luxury details.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive fit that familiar utility-vehicle layout. The Mesa’s appeal is in the straightforward appearance: it looks more at home with a little dust on the body than a velvet rope beside it. For a change of scene from the city, it sets the right mood. Keep the dress shoes in the closet and let the route become part of the day."],
  "coil-raiden": ["The Coil Raiden gives GTA VI a clean, modern sedan shaped by the Tesla Model S. Its smooth roofline and restrained bodywork make a change from the vents, scoops and chrome competing for attention elsewhere in the garage.", "With four seats and all-wheel drive, the Raiden has the layout of a contemporary all-weather sedan. Visually, it keeps things calm: a low nose, a flowing cabin and very little ornament. That restraint is its own kind of statement. If your taste leans toward modern design rather than mechanical theater, this Coil fits the brief without needing to turn every trip into an announcement."],
  "declasse-granger": ["The Declasse Granger has the scale and long-roof silhouette of a Chevrolet Suburban-inspired SUV in GTA VI. Its long roof, tall cabin and broad body give it the look of a full-size American SUV, the sort of vehicle that makes neighboring cars seem to have arrived in a smaller size.", "The Granger’s appeal is straightforward utility styling rather than showroom theatrics. Its all-wheel-drive layout sits beneath a body with the familiar proportions of a family hauler or fleet vehicle. For players who like a convoy aesthetic, it has the right outline without needing to be dressed as anything special. Even parked alone, it looks as though the rest of the group might arrive shortly."],
  "declasse-granger-3600lx": ["The Declasse Granger 3600LX updates the Granger formula with styling inspired by the 2015–2020 Chevrolet Suburban. In GTA VI, its cleaner surfaces and more contemporary front end give the familiar full-size SUV shape a sharper, more polished appearance.", "All-wheel drive accompanies a long, substantial body that still puts presence ahead of delicacy. The 3600LX suits players who want the scale of a traditional American SUV with a more modern finish. It looks at home outside a business venue or lined up with the crew’s other cars. The footprint is generous; anyone calling it compact is probably standing next to a building."],
  "declasse-impaler-80": ["The Declasse Impaler ’80 captures an unmistakable era of American sedan design in GTA VI, with the sixth-generation Chevrolet Impala as its reference. Its upright cabin, long trunk and straight body lines capture a familiar era of American sedan design, when a ruler was apparently the most important tool in the studio.", "This is the boxier side of the Impaler family, with a different visual character from the rounded Impaler SZ. The appeal lies in that simple, substantial outline: a car that looks entirely natural outside a diner, beside a motel or in a collection of older American metal. It has presence without needing to look expensive."],
  "declasse-impaler-sz": ["The Declasse Impaler SZ ’95 takes the 1994–1996 Chevrolet Impala SS as its reference point, bringing a broad, rounded American sedan shape to GTA VI. The long body and restrained styling give it a muscular look without turning it into a two-door coupe.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive suit that traditional sports-sedan arrangement. Compared with the angular Impaler ’80, the SZ has a softer outline and a more distinctly ’90s character. It’s an appealing choice for anyone who likes American cars with a little understatement. There’s plenty of attitude in the proportions; a giant wing would mostly interrupt the conversation."],
  "declasse-mamba-gt": ["Long hood, low roof, old-school racing shape. The Declasse Mamba GT ’64 brings vintage GT coupe style to GTA VI, drawing on the Shelby Daytona Coupe’s design. Its closed cockpit and low bodywork put that classic racing character front and center.", "The appeal starts with the proportions: a stretched nose, a compact cabin and a silhouette that feels closer to a paddock photograph than an everyday parking lot. For a garage with a taste for historic race-car design, the Mamba GT looks right at home. It has enough visual drama to make standing still seem like an occasion."],
  "declasse-moonbeam": ["A classic-car collection can make room for a van. In GTA VI, the Declasse Moonbeam takes its shape from the first-generation Chevrolet Astro and GMC Safari. Its short nose, tall cabin and square body give it a familiar neighborhood presence, far removed from the low-slung coupes around it.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout straightforward. The Moonbeam’s character comes from that unapologetic van shape, with plenty of broad bodywork and very little interest in pretending to be a sports car. It adds variety to a collection and looks perfectly comfortable at a casual meet. Someone has to bring the folding chairs."],
  "declasse-tulip": ["The Declasse Tulip ’72 gives GTA VI a four-door take on early-’70s American muscle. Its design draws on the 1972 Chevrolet Chevelle Malibu and Oldsmobile Cutlass Supreme, combining a long hood with the extra cabin length of a sedan.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive make this a different proposition visually from the two-door classics beside it. The Tulip keeps the period shape and muscular proportions without asking the rest of the crew to find another ride. Its charm is in that slightly unexpected combination: family-car doors, old-school American attitude. It looks like the sensible choice until you remember what everyone else in the garage considers sensible."],
  "declasse-tulip-m-100": ["The Declasse Tulip M-100 ’78 takes its styling from the fourth-generation Chevrolet Malibu, giving GTA VI a squared-off American coupe with a distinctly later-era look. The straighter roofline and cleaner body panels set it apart from the earlier, four-door Tulip.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive suit the simple coupe layout. There’s an appealing lack of ceremony to the M-100: familiar proportions, a proper trunk and just enough muscle-car character to make the shape interesting. It fits a collection built around overlooked American classics rather than obvious poster cars. Some cars enter the meet with a speech prepared. This one can just park."],
  "declasse-vamos": ["The Declasse Vamos ’74 puts Chevrolet Nova-inspired muscle into a relatively compact coupe body in GTA VI. Its straightforward body lines and traditional long-hood proportions give it a more modest-looking footprint than some of the grander American classics.", "With two seats and rear-wheel drive, the Vamos keeps the familiar formula simple. The design has a working-class quality that suits a garage full of cars chosen for character rather than ceremony. There’s enough shape to enjoy without layers of ornament getting in the way. For anyone who likes the idea of an old American coupe outside a small neighborhood workshop, the Vamos fits the picture."],
  "declasse-vigero-zx-convertible": ["The Declasse Vigero ZX Convertible combines sixth-generation Chevrolet Camaro-inspired styling with an open-top profile in GTA VI. The broad shoulders and sharply drawn front end keep the modern muscle-car character intact, while the convertible body changes the mood.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive sit beneath the aggressive styling. This is a car that looks ready for a warm evening, a coastal road and a destination chosen mostly because the route is good. The appeal is in that combination of visual muscle and open-air atmosphere. You can dress it up as a serious automotive decision, but the weather probably deserves some of the credit."],
  "declasse-walton-l35-stock": ["The Declasse Walton ’81 is a compact pickup in GTA VI, with styling drawn mainly from the first-generation Chevrolet S-10 (1982–1993). The boxy cab, short bed and upright front end give it the plain, working-truck look of an older small pickup.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive carry over from the Walton L35 Stock of GTA Online. It is a different truck from the older Walton seen in San Andreas and Vice City, and it looks more at home on a coastal back road than in a showroom."],
  "declasse-yosemite-1500": ["The Declasse Yosemite 1500 is a full-size pickup in GTA VI, based mainly on the 1999–2002 Chevrolet Silverado 1500. Its squared-off cab, wide stance and flared wheel arches give it the proportions of a turn-of-the-millennium American work truck.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive carry over from GTA Online, where the Yosemite 1500 first appeared. It suits drivers who want their pickup to look capable rather than polished, and it leaves the chrome to someone else."],
  "dinka-blista-compact": ["Small body, recognizable shape: the Dinka Blista ’85 takes its design cues from the first-generation Honda CR-X in GTA VI. Its small hatchback body, short overhangs and simple lines give it an entirely different presence from the wide coupes and oversized SUVs around it. Earlier games called it the Blista Compact.", "Two seats and front-wheel drive keep the layout true to the compact-car idea. The appeal is in the proportions and the familiar ’80s Japanese look, with a shape that feels at home in a collection of older imports. The Blista doesn’t need a dramatic entrance to have character. At a meet full of cars occupying a space and a half, simply fitting between the lines has its own dignity."],
  "dinka-sugoi": ["Subtlety was clearly optional when it came to the Dinka Sugoi’s design. This GTA VI hot hatch takes its angular styling from the Honda Civic Type R FK8. Its angular body and assertive detailing give the practical hatchback shape a much louder visual personality than its everyday origins might suggest.", "Four seats and front-wheel drive keep the underlying arrangement familiar. The Sugoi’s appeal is the way it wears its enthusiasm openly: a modern Japanese hatch that looks like it would rather be at a meet than waiting outside the shops. For players drawn to sharp lines and a little excess, the design has plenty to say. Nobody in the styling department seems to have asked for fewer angles."],
  "dundreary-landstalker-xl": ["The Dundreary Landstalker XL takes the fourth-generation Lincoln Navigator as its styling reference, bringing full-size American luxury to GTA VI. Its long roof, substantial cabin and formal front end create a more polished presence than the rugged image of a traditional utility SUV.", "With four seats and all-wheel drive, the Landstalker XL has a familiar layout beneath all that bodywork. It suits players who like their luxury cars upright, spacious-looking and difficult to overlook. The design works well for a dressed-up night out or a collection built around executive cars. The XL badge is refreshingly honest about how much of the driveway is involved."],
  "dundreary-regina": ["The Dundreary Regina is a long-roof piece of Americana in GTA VI, with Chevrolet Caprice wagon influences. Its long roof and upright rear body turn the traditional full-size sedan shape into a station wagon with plenty of period character.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive give the Regina a straightforward layout. Its charm is in the ordinary details: the sort of car that looks as though it has spent years outside suburban houses, roadside diners and places selling very large breakfasts. In a garage full of performance-looking machinery, the wagon makes a welcome change. It has the visual energy of a family vacation whose directions were printed before anyone left."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026: confirmed unchanged, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "sirius-transgressor-67": ["A long hood and a dressed-up coupe shape define the Sirius Transgressor ’67 in GTA VI, drawing on the 1970 Mercury Cougar. Its classic American coupe proportions sit between muscle-car attitude and a more dressed-up personal-luxury look, giving it a distinct place among the older cars.", "The attraction is in the shape: a substantial nose, a compact-looking cabin and a body that lets the lines run without too much interruption. The Transgressor suits a collection where classic styling matters as much as a familiar name. It has the right mood for a quiet evening meet, when there’s time to walk around the cars instead of immediately talking about numbers."],
  "emperor-vectre": ["Sculpted surfaces give the Emperor Vectre a distinct identity among GTA VI’s Japanese-inspired coupes. The Lexus RC F is its main design reference. Its sculpted body, assertive nose and compact cabin give it a more modern, carefully shaped appearance than the squared-off Japanese classics nearby.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive define the layout, while the design balances luxury-coupe proportions with a more aggressive expression. The Vectre suits players who like Japanese cars but want something beyond the familiar ’90s tuner silhouette. It looks polished without losing its edge, and distinctive without needing a history lesson. At a meet, this is the coupe for someone who appreciates an old Skyline but arrived wearing a newer jacket."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "ascot-paragon": ["The Ascot Paragon follows the grand-touring proportions of the 2018 Bentley Continental GT in GTA VI. A substantial nose, smooth roofline and broad coupe body give it a relaxed sense of status, with more emphasis on elegance than spectacle. GTA Online players knew it as the Enus Paragon R; in GTA VI it wears the Ascot badge.", "The Paragon’s visual appeal is in how naturally it combines a sporting outline with luxury-car presence. It suits a garage where the cars are expected to look good outside a hotel as well as under workshop lights. There’s nothing wrong with making an entrance that suggests you read the dress code and then improved on it."],
  "fathom-fr36": ["The Fathom FR36 gives GTA VI a Japanese sports coupe with unmistakable early-2000s energy. Its design is rooted in the Infiniti G35 Coupe, also sold as the Nissan Skyline V35, with touches from the later Infiniti G37 and Nissan 350Z. The shape is clean, familiar and ready for a build without arriving half-finished.", "With two seats and rear-wheel drive, the FR36 follows the classic front-engine coupe formula. It fits the driver who wants a street car with real tuner presence rather than another low-slung exotic. Keep the setup clean or lean into the era—the body already has enough character to carry either direction."],
  // 2026-11-20 (Fausto): in GTA VI it is just the "Baller" (only Baller and Baller ST-D exist); name updated provisionally, Codex review pending.
  "gallivanter-baller-ii": ["Range Rover Sport-inspired proportions give the Gallivanter Baller a familiar luxury SUV silhouette in GTA VI. Its upright body and clean proportions balance a substantial appearance with the more polished character of a modern British SUV. GTA V had an older Baller and a newer Baller II; this GTA VI Baller is the newer Baller II design under a shorter name.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive provide the familiar layout. The Baller occupies the middle ground between an overtly rugged utility vehicle and something dressed entirely for the valet stand. That versatility is visual as much as anything: it can set the mood for a weekend away or simply look established outside an expensive address. The car is comfortable with either image, even if its owner has only packed for one."],
  "gallivanter-baller-st-d": ["The Gallivanter Baller ST-D takes its visual lead from the fifth-generation Range Rover L460. In GTA VI, its smooth body surfaces and restrained detailing give the luxury SUV shape a cleaner, more contemporary expression than the earlier Ballers.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive sit beneath the substantial outline. The ST-D’s appeal is in its restraint: a car can look imposing without covering every panel in vents and decoration. It belongs in a modern luxury collection, especially if you like the idea of a large SUV that doesn’t need to advertise every design decision. The name may invite jokes; the styling keeps a straight face."],
  "grotti-carbonizzare": ["The Grotti Carbonizzare brings a long-nosed, open-top sports-car shape to GTA VI, with Aston Martin V12 Zagato influences in its design. The curved bodywork and compact cabin give it a more flowing appearance than Grotti’s sharper, wedge-shaped classics.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive suit the familiar roadster layout. Its appeal is in the balance between an elegant outline and a little visual drama, making it a natural fit for a warm evening drive through the city. The Carbonizzare looks like a car chosen because the owner enjoys looking back at it after parking. That is a perfectly respectable selection process."],
  "grotti-cheetah-95": ["Wide, low and unapologetically theatrical, the Grotti Cheetah ’95 mixes Ferrari Testarossa and 512 BB influences in GTA VI. Its angular proportions and distinctive side treatment give it the presence of a car that belonged on a bedroom wall before it belonged in a garage. In GTA Online it went by Cheetah Classic.", "The appeal is unmistakably old-school: broad bodywork, a compact cabin and a silhouette with very little interest in practicality. For a collection built around classic supercar shapes, the Cheetah ’95 is an obvious talking point. It looks especially at home in the city after dark, when the surroundings finally become as theatrical as the car."],
  "piccia-furia": ["The Piccia Furia mixes modern Italian supercar influences in GTA VI: Ferrari 488 Pista cues at the front, SF90 Stradale inspiration at the rear and elements of the Pininfarina Battista in the side profile. The result is a low, sculpted shape with plenty happening from every angle. The Furia was a Grotti in GTA Online and now carries the new Piccia name.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive complete the layout. Visually, the Furia sits at the modern end of supercar design, where deep curves and layered surfaces replace the simpler wedges of older exotics. It’s a car for players who enjoy the design details as much as the overall silhouette. One quick walk around it rarely stays quick."],
  "grotti-itali-rsx": ["The Grotti Itali RSX brings modern Italian supercar drama to GTA VI. Its shape is led by the Ferrari SF90 Stradale, while the rear draws from the Ferrari F8 Tributo and the headlights echo the limited-run Ferrari SP38. The result is sharp without turning every panel into a separate argument.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive sit beneath the low, sculpted body. The RSX belongs in a garage built around contemporary exotics, polished paint and arrivals that deserve a second look. It can handle the expensive part of town just fine. Finding a parking space worthy of it may take longer."],
  "imponte-df8-90": ["The Imponte DF8-90 has a distinctly Pontiac-flavored identity in GTA VI, drawing on the G6 and Grand Am. Its rounded body and conventional four-door proportions give it the look of an American sedan trying to add a little excitement to the weekday routine.", "The DF8-90’s appeal is less about luxury and more about a recognizable period of everyday car design. It has enough shape to stand apart from anonymous traffic without adopting a supercar’s wardrobe. For a garage that includes ordinary-looking cars with personality, this Imponte fills a useful visual gap. Sometimes the interesting choice is the one nobody put on a poster."],
  "imponte-phoenix": ["The Imponte Phoenix ’77 wears its American muscle-car roots openly in GTA VI, with second-generation Pontiac Firebird and Chevrolet Camaro influences. Its long hood, low cabin and broad rear quarters give it the distinctive outline of an American pony car with a taste for attention.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout straightforward. The Phoenix’s appeal is in that dramatic body shape, where even an ordinary street corner can become a convincing backdrop. It suits players who like their classics a little louder visually than a restrained coupe. There’s a certain confidence to a car that looks ready for a period movie poster before anyone has chosen the paint."],
  "imponte-ruiner": ["The Imponte Ruiner ’82 takes Pontiac Trans Am and Chevrolet Camaro cues and turns them into GTA VI’s kind of angular American coupe. Its low nose and straight-edged profile have a distinctly ’80s feel, with less of the rounded bodywork found on earlier muscle cars.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive sit beneath the familiar shape. The Ruiner’s charm is partly in how firmly it belongs to its era: the sort of car that looks right beside an old workshop or under the lights at a late-night meet. It doesn’t require a complicated explanation. If the silhouette makes you think of cassette tapes, you’re already on the right track."],
  "invetero-coquette": ["The Invetero Coquette’s long hood and sharp bodywork point toward the Chevrolet Corvette C7 Stingray, its design inspiration in GTA VI. Its long hood, rear-set cabin and broad shoulders give it a recognizably American sports-car profile, with sharper surfaces than the older generations that inspired the Coquette name.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the arrangement focused. The appeal is in the balance of familiar proportions and modern detailing: low enough to look special, substantial enough to carry some visual muscle. This is the regular Coquette rather than the D10, and the different silhouette is worth appreciating. In a garage full of American cars, it marks a clear shift from muscle coupe to sports car."],
  "invetero-coquette-d10": ["The Invetero Coquette D10 takes the Chevrolet Corvette C8 as its design reference and gives GTA VI a more exotic-looking American sports car. The shorter nose, forward-looking cabin placement and prominent rear bodywork create a noticeably different silhouette from the regular Coquette.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive preserve the focused layout. The D10’s attraction is that change in visual character: recognizably part of the Coquette family, but shaped more like something you would expect among European exotics. It suits a modern sports-car collection where the proportions matter as much as the badge. American design has clearly found another way to make an entrance."],
  "karin-asterope-gz": ["The Karin Asterope GZ finds its character in an everyday shape. This GTA VI sedan draws on the Toyota Camry XV30. It’s a familiar shape, and that familiarity is a large part of its character.", "The design keeps the drama low: a proper trunk, a roomy-looking cabin and very little ornament trying to explain why it belongs at a car meet. For players who enjoy ordinary cars as much as poster material, the Asterope GZ has its own appeal. It looks like it should be returning a rental agreement, which makes finding one in an enthusiast’s garage all the more charming."],
  "karin-contender": ["The Karin Contender brings a heavily styled pickup shape to GTA VI, drawing on the Toyota Tundra-based Devolro Diablo and Ford F-150 Raptor. Its tall body and substantial front end give it a more assertive look than an ordinary work truck.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive sit beneath the crew-cab proportions. The Contender’s appeal is in the mix of pickup utility styling and show-truck presence, with enough bodywork to make a normal parking bay look like a suggestion. It suits a garage with a taste for lifted-truck aesthetics and weekends away from the city. A little dust would hardly look out of place."],
  "karin-feroci": ["Rounded rather than sharply creased, the Karin Feroci ’98 captures first-generation Lexus GS 300 styling in GTA VI. Its curved roofline and rounded four-door body capture the look of a Japanese executive sedan from an era before every surface needed a sharp crease.", "The appeal is understated, with a shape that feels established rather than eager to impress. The Feroci fits naturally among older Japanese sedans and coupes, offering a more formal silhouette without losing the character of its period. It’s a car for players who notice the quieter entries in a parking lot. A clean design can make its point without borrowing a wing from a race car."],
  "karin-futo": ["Toyota AE86 Levin influence is easy to recognize in GTA VI’s Karin Futo ’85. Its square body, compact proportions and straightforward front end give it the familiar look of an ’80s Japanese car that enthusiasts still find room for in a crowded garage.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive form the simple layout beneath the bodywork. The Futo’s character comes from that modest scale and unmistakable period shape, not from looking expensive. It belongs in a lineup of older imports, especially when the owners care more about the cars than the dress code. There’s something reassuring about a coupe that looks perfectly happy outside a small workshop."],
  "karin-intruder": ["Infiniti Q45 and I30 influences shape the Karin Intruder, a restrained Japanese sedan in GTA VI. Its conventional roofline and clean four-door body give it the kind of executive-car presence that works without a large grille doing all the talking.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout familiar. The Intruder’s appeal is its quiet visual confidence, making it a good fit for a collection of Japanese cars with a more mature style. It looks equally plausible outside an office or beside a row of carefully kept imports. Not every interesting car needs to introduce itself from the other end of the street."],
  "karin-rebel": ["The Karin Rebel ’84 is a compact old-school pickup in GTA VI, shaped closely around the fourth-generation Toyota Hilux SR5 XtraCab. Its square cab, simple bed and upright front come from an era when a truck could look useful without covering every surface in plastic armor.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive keep the Rebel’s layout as straightforward as its bodywork. It suits back roads, rough ground and garages where a few scratches count as history rather than damage. Some trucks arrive with a lifestyle campaign. This one looks ready to get on with the job."],
  "emperor-sultan": ["The Emperor Sultan combines Lexus IS, Mitsubishi Lancer Evolution VI and Subaru Impreza influences in GTA VI. Its compact four-door shape sits between Japanese sports-sedan styling and the visual language of rally-bred road cars. Returning players will remember the Sultan as a Karin; GTA VI moves it to Emperor.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive give the Sultan a layout that will be familiar to returning players. The attraction is the blend: enough everyday sedan in the body to look grounded, enough sporting character to make the name worth remembering. This is the standard Sultan, with its own proportions and identity. For a garage built around Japanese cars, it’s the kind of shape that makes sense without a lengthy sales pitch."],
  "karin-vivanite": ["The Karin Vivanite gives GTA VI’s streets a familiar family-car silhouette, taking its design cues from the fourth-generation Toyota Sienna XL40. Its long cabin and family-car proportions make it an unusual sight among the sports coupes and muscle cars that tend to dominate an enthusiast’s garage.", "That’s part of the appeal. The Vivanite has the recognizable shape of everyday transportation, with a more contemporary face than the older vans around it. It’s a choice for players who enjoy a little variety and don’t need every vehicle to look like a track-day invitation. At a meet full of dramatic entrances, arriving in a minivan is its own small act of confidence."],
  "maibatsu-penumbra": ["The Maibatsu Penumbra mixes Mitsubishi Eclipse and Audi TT influences in GTA VI, giving it a rounded sports-coupe shape with a distinctly different look from the boxier Japanese classics. The arched cabin and broad body surfaces carry more of the design than sharp creases or busy trim.", "It’s a two-seat, rear-wheel-drive coupe with a familiar place in the import-car side of GTA. The Penumbra works well for players who like the softer styling of a later generation of coupes. Park it beside an Elegy ’90 and the contrast is part of the fun: two different ideas of what an enthusiast’s Japanese car should look like."],
  "maibatsu-penumbra-ff": ["The Maibatsu Penumbra FF ’97 brings one of tuner culture’s most recognizable shapes into GTA VI. Its main influence is the second-generation Mitsubishi Eclipse, supported by Nissan Skyline R33-inspired headlights and a front bumper that recalls the Honda Integra Type R. The result lands squarely in the era of bold kits, bright paint and parking-lot debates.", "This two-seat, all-wheel-drive coupe has the compact proportions to look convincing as a clean street build or something far less restrained. The Penumbra FF does not need to explain why the late ’90s still matter. Anyone who already stopped scrolling probably knows."],
  "mammoth-patriot-mil-spec": ["The Mammoth Patriot Mil-Spec gives GTA VI the broad stance and military roots of the Hummer H1, finished with cues from Mil-Spec Automotive’s custom H1 builds. Its flat body panels, wide track and near-vertical surfaces make most modern SUVs look as though they dressed for the wrong occasion.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive make room for the crew beneath all that visual armor. The Patriot Mil-Spec suits off-road routes, convoy duty and any entrance where subtlety has already been ruled out. It is large, square and completely comfortable with both facts."],
  "obey-8f-drafter": ["The Obey 8F Drafter takes its cues from the 2018 Audi RS5 Coupe, bringing a clean German two-door profile to GTA VI. A broad nose and tightly drawn body lines give it a sporting expression without abandoning the proportions of a conventional coupe.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive complete the layout. The 8F Drafter has a polished, modern look that works well among both luxury cars and more overtly styled sports models. It’s the kind of car you choose when you enjoy the details but don’t need every panel to explain itself. A sharp jacket, an evening in the city and a parking space with decent lighting would suit it."],
  "obey-tailgater-s": ["Compact proportions and an assertive nose give the Obey Tailgater S its identity in GTA VI. Its design takes cues from the Audi RS3 Sedan. Its assertive nose and tightly proportioned body give it a compact, sporting character.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive provide the familiar layout, while the exterior has the look of a modern sports sedan. The Tailgater S suits a collection of contemporary German-inspired cars, especially if you prefer something that keeps a conventional roofline and a proper trunk. It looks dressed for everyday use, but with the sort of expression that suggests the owner spends a little too much time choosing wheels."],
  "ocelot-jugular": ["The Ocelot Jugular takes the Jaguar XE SV Project 8 as its styling reference, giving GTA VI a British sports sedan with a more assertive shape than an ordinary executive car. The familiar four-door outline is still there, but the body carries a noticeably more muscular attitude.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive complete the layout. The Jugular makes a good visual companion to modern coupes without needing to hide its sedan proportions. It’s a choice for players who like the idea of something practical-looking with a less practical sense of restraint. The name is dramatic, but the design makes a reasonably strong case for keeping it."],
  "ocelot-locust": ["The Ocelot Locust takes its inspiration from the Lotus 3-Eleven, bringing an exposed-cockpit sports-car shape to GTA VI. The low body and minimal upper structure leave very little between the occupants and the surrounding scenery.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive suit the stripped-back layout. Visually, the Locust belongs closer to a paddock than a hotel entrance, with the sort of purposeful simplicity that makes more elaborate sports cars look overdressed. It’s a distinctive addition to a collection built around unusual driver-focused shapes. Pack lightly in spirit, at least; this is not a car whose appearance suggests an enthusiasm for luggage or small talk."],
  "pegassi-infernus-classic": ["The Pegassi Infernus ’96 brings peak poster-car energy to GTA VI. Its wedge-shaped body is led by the Lamborghini Diablo, with Cizeta-Moroder V16T influence around the sides and rear and a Ferrari Testarossa flavor at the front. Add the pop-up headlights and the decade is no longer difficult to place. GTA Online listed it as the Infernus Classic.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive complete the classic exotic layout. The Infernus belongs on coastal roads, outside expensive hotels and in any garage that still respects a properly dramatic silhouette. Visibility may not be its strongest social skill, but being ignored will never be a problem."],
  "pegassi-tempesta": ["The Pegassi Tempesta combines Lamborghini Huracán and Centenario influences into a low, compact supercar shape in GTA VI. Its low wedge profile, compact cabin and sharp bodywork give it the unmistakable presence of a modern Italian exotic.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive sit beneath the angular shape. The Tempesta’s design is direct enough to read at a glance, but the proportions still reward a closer look: low at the front, broad around the rear and tightly wrapped around the cabin. It suits players who want a recognizable supercar silhouette without needing an especially complicated story behind it. The shape does a perfectly good job of starting the conversation."],
  "pegassi-toros": ["The Pegassi Toros takes Lamborghini Urus-inspired SUV styling and mixes in cues from the Aventador and Audi Q8. In GTA VI, the result is a tall, broad vehicle wearing some of the sharp-edged visual language usually reserved for exotics.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive give it the familiar SUV layout, but the expression is anything but reserved. The Toros suits players who like modern luxury trucks with a strong sports-car influence. It looks ready for an expensive driveway, a late-night meet or a very unnecessary entrance at the coffee shop. Apparently, choosing an SUV doesn’t have to mean choosing fewer angles."],
  // progen-emerus: Codex RS-0073 (Neue-Fahrzeuge-Emerus-GranForma-Zorrusso-2026-10-16.md + Emerus-Nachweis-2026-10-16.md: Launch Trailer 0:46 sentence). Senna stated as our own knowledge, no source attribution (Fausto 16.10.).
  "progen-emerus": ["The Emerus appears in GTA VI’s Launch Trailer, with a green-and-white example crossing the frame at 0:46. Its design draws on the McLaren Senna, which puts the emphasis on a very particular kind of exotic: the track-day poster car, where a low stance and an appetite for aero matter more than looking discreet outside a restaurant.", "The Emerus name already has history in GTA Online, where Rockstar introduced it under Progen. For GTA VI, that familiar identity is a useful point of reference rather than a substitute for checking the new car. The appeal is the competition-minded look: something for the enthusiast who notices the hardware before the paint. Its place in the next generation of GTA’s car culture is worth following without borrowing the old game’s performance figures."],
  // granforma-zorrusso: Codex Launch B8 (20.11.2026), approved by Fausto 20.11. Earlier: Codex RS-0073 (Neue-Fahrzeuge-Emerus-GranForma-Zorrusso-2026-10-16.md), approved by Fausto 16.10. (values = Pegassi Zorrusso, same car).
  "granforma-zorrusso": ["The Zorrusso’s Italdesign Zerouno-inspired drama comes with a new detail to inspect in GTA VI: different rear lettering and an unfamiliar emblem. The low body and layered surfaces still give you plenty to look at around the rear quarters, but the branding now deserves a closer look of its own.", "The GranForma name first drew attention in the Rockstar images published with Bloomberg’s October 14 feature. The in-game make is GranForma, replacing the Pegassi identity familiar from GTA Online. For collectors, that gives an established shape a different place in the manufacturer garage."],
  "pfister-astron": ["Porsche Macan-inspired curves give the Pfister Astron its distinctive SUV profile in GTA VI. Its rounded front and gently tapering profile create a less upright shape than the larger luxury trucks.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive provide the familiar layout. The Astron looks like a natural companion to the Comets and Growlers in a Pfister-focused collection, with enough family resemblance to make the change of body style feel deliberate. It suits players who want an SUV with a more restrained sporting appearance. There’s room in the garage for something taller without abandoning the aesthetic."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "pfister-comet-retro-custom": ["The Pfister Comet ’88 brings the look of a RAUH-Welt-inspired Porsche 911 into GTA VI, with the classic 930 shape as its starting point. The wide body and rounded cabin give it a very different presence from the cleaner lines of a modern Comet. GTA Online players will recognize it as the Comet Retro Custom.", "This is a car whose visual character comes from contrast: an older silhouette with a much more assertive stance. It belongs among classic sports cars and tuner builds in equal measure."],
  "pfister-comet-s2-cabrio": ["The Pfister Comet S2 pairs a familiar sports-car silhouette with an open roof in GTA VI, drawing on the Porsche 911 Turbo S Cabriolet. Its familiar rounded nose, compact cabin and broad rear body translate the modern 911 shape into an open-top sports car. GTA Online had the Comet S2 and a separate Comet S2 Cabrio; GTA VI has a single Comet S2.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout focused. The Comet S2’s character is in the combination of a recognizable sports-car silhouette and a more relaxed visual mood. It looks right on a coastal road or parked beside a café long after the original plan was to leave. Some cars make you invent a reason to drive them. With this one, a warm evening is a fairly convincing argument."],
  "pfister-growler": ["The Pfister Growler takes the Porsche 718 Cayman as its design reference, giving GTA VI a compact sports coupe with a clean, rounded profile. Its proportions are tighter and less expansive than the larger exotics, with a cabin that feels neatly contained within the body.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive complete the straightforward layout. The Growler’s appeal is its sense of visual focus: a sports-car shape without much ornament getting between you and the lines. It suits players who enjoy a car that looks purposeful without making every surface an announcement. In a collection full of dramatic machinery, a little restraint can become the distinctive feature."],
  "pfister-neon": ["The Pfister Neon gives GTA VI a sleek electric sports sedan shaped by the Porsche Mission E concept that became the Taycan. Its front also carries Porsche 918 Spyder influence, while the rear borrows from the Panamera and modern 911. It looks unmistakably Pfister without needing an air-cooled history lesson.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive place the Neon between practical sedan and modern performance car. Its smooth body and low roofline suit a clean, technology-focused garage where noise is optional but presence is not. Bring friends, leave the exhaust debate to everyone else."],
  "schyster-deviant": ["The Schyster Deviant ’72 draws on the 1972 AMC Javelin, bringing a less predictable slice of American muscle-car design to GTA VI. Its long hood, curved rear quarters and distinctive coupe profile offer something different from the more familiar Mustang- and Challenger-inspired shapes.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout conventional. The Deviant’s character is in the body: substantial, expressive and slightly outside the usual muscle-car conversation. It suits a collection chosen with personal taste rather than a checklist of famous names. At a meet, this is the sort of car that makes someone pause, look again and ask a better question than how much it cost."],
  "schyster-pmp-700": ["Broad and upright, the Schyster PMP 700 takes its sedan styling from the second-generation Chrysler 300 in GTA VI. Its broad sedan body, upright front and formal roofline give it a strong American luxury-car presence without resorting to a coupe’s low silhouette.", "The design is all about visual weight and a confident outline. It looks at home outside an office building, a late-night restaurant or anywhere the owner would like to appear slightly more established than the paperwork suggests. The PMP 700 suits players who enjoy large sedans with character. Four-door elegance doesn’t have to be delicate, and this Schyster makes that point before anyone has opened a door."],
  "truffade-thrax": ["The Truffade Thrax brings Bugatti Divo and Italdesign Zerouno influences to GTA VI, combining a broad hypercar body with sharply sculpted detailing. The low cabin and substantial rear section give it a sense of scale that photographs need a person nearby to explain.", "Two seats and all-wheel drive sit beneath the elaborate shape. The Thrax’s visual character is unapologetically extravagant, with very little of the restraint found in a simple sports coupe. It suits a collection where the design is allowed to become an event. Even a routine trip across town looks as though it should have involved an invitation and a carefully worded dress code."],
  "ubermacht-cypher": ["The Übermacht Cypher builds on BMW M2 F87-inspired proportions, with additional BMW M6 F13 and M8 F92 design cues. In GTA VI, the result is a compact sports coupe with a broad stance and a more muscular body than its size first suggests.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the layout focused. The Cypher’s visual character is in that tightly packed shape: a short-looking cabin, substantial shoulders and enough detail to make a walk around it worthwhile. It suits a modern German-inspired collection, particularly if you prefer your coupe to look purposeful without stretching across half the driveway."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "ubermacht-sentinel-classic": ["Straight lines, an upright nose, and compact proportions give the Übermacht Sentinel ’85 its familiar BMW E30 character. The design takes its cues from the E30 M3, with the tidy, squared-off shape that made this generation a favorite among fans of older German cars.", "In GTA VI, the Sentinel ’85 is a convertible with a roof you can close. Open or closed, it keeps the restrained look of a small German classic rather than the longer, more elaborate shape of a grand tourer."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "ubermacht-zion": ["The Übermacht Apoc brings the broad proportions of the BMW 6 Series and M6 of the E63/E64 era to GTA VI. A long hood and substantial rear body give it a more expansive shape than Übermacht’s compact classics. This is German grand-touring style with a little room to stretch.", "GTA V and GTA Online split the design between the Zion and Zion Cabrio. GTA VI brings them together as the Apoc, a convertible with a roof you can close. The open cabin suits a coastal drive, while the body keeps the presence of a large luxury coupe. It does not need a supercar silhouette to look expensive."],
  "vapid-aleutian": ["The Vapid Aleutian takes its styling from the fourth-generation Ford Expedition, bringing a substantial American SUV shape to GTA VI. Its tall cabin, broad front and long body have the familiar proportions of a full-size family hauler with a more assertive expression.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive provide the underlying layout. The Aleutian looks well suited to a collection of modern trucks and large sedans, with the kind of presence that makes a convoy aesthetic easy to picture. It also looks like the vehicle someone volunteers when a small group plans a weekend away. The group stays small; the vehicle clearly declined."],
  "vapid-caracara-4x4": ["The Vapid Caracara 4x4 brings Ford F-150 Raptor presence to GTA VI. Its design draws heavily from the second-generation Raptor, with a broad crew-cab body, raised stance and the kind of front end that makes smaller traffic reconsider its lane choice.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive give the Caracara 4x4 room for the crew behind all that truck. It suits mud trails, off-road gatherings and a garage where clean paint is more of a temporary condition. The six-wheel Caracara may be the louder relative, but this one hardly looks short on confidence."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "dundreary-chino-65": ["The Dundreary Chino ’65 blends 1965 Lincoln Continental and Chrysler Imperial influences into GTA VI’s classic-car lineup. Its long, straight body and formal roofline create an American coupe with a more dressed-up character than the usual muscle-car shape. In GTA V and GTA Online the Chino was a Vapid, so the Dundreary badge is new.", "The Chino ’65 looks right at a relaxed meet, where there’s time to appreciate the body lines and the way a little trim changes the whole profile. It has the presence of a car from an era when parking spaces were apparently somebody else’s problem."],
  "vapid-dominator": ["The Vapid Dominator is a familiar piece of American pony-car design in GTA VI, shaped by the Ford Mustang. Its long hood, compact cabin and broad rear quarters create a familiar modern American muscle-car outline, with enough retro influence to connect it to the older coupes.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the arrangement straightforward. This is the standard Dominator, distinct from the ASP, GT and GTX, and its simpler shape is a large part of the appeal. It makes a natural starting point for a collection of American cars without needing an explanation of limited editions or special packages. Sometimes the familiar name and the right proportions are already enough."],
  "vapid-dominator-asp": ["New Edge Mustang fans have a recognizable shape in the Vapid Dominator ASP. This GTA VI coupe takes its styling cues from the Ford Mustang SVT Cobra R. The sharper body lines and compact-looking cabin give it a distinctly different character from the more retro-shaped standard Dominator.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive sit beneath the familiar pony-car proportions. The ASP occupies a particular corner of American car culture: modern enough to feel different from the older classics, old enough to carry a strong identity of its own. It suits players who know exactly which Mustang era they like. At a meet, the right people will recognize the shape before the conversation reaches the badge."],
  "vapid-dominator-gt": ["The Vapid Dominator GT puts 2018–2023 Ford Mustang Convertible-inspired design into GTA VI’s open-top lineup. The long hood and broad body retain the familiar modern pony-car character, while the open-top profile gives it a more easygoing visual mood.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive keep the arrangement simple. The GT suits a drive where the scenery matters and the destination is negotiable, especially with the city lights coming on at the end of a warm day. It’s a different kind of occasion from the closed coupes in the Dominator family. Same interest in American muscle styling, slightly stronger interest in the weather forecast."],
  "vapid-ganado-70": ["Part classic coupe, part pickup, the Vapid Ganado ’70 mixes 1970 Ford Ranchero and 1969–1970 Mercury Cougar influences in GTA VI. Its car-derived pickup shape combines a long coupe-like nose with an open rear bed, giving it a different character from a conventional truck.", "The Ganado sits in that appealing space between American muscle styling and everyday utility. Its lines look right beside older coupes, but the rear half tells a different story. For a garage with a taste for unusual classics, it’s an easy shape to appreciate. It looks like someone wanted a weekend car and a work vehicle, then negotiated a very stylish compromise."],
  "vapid-montagne": ["The Vapid Montagne takes a familiar modern SUV shape into GTA VI, drawing on the sixth-generation Ford Explorer. Its modern SUV body combines a tall cabin with a more tapered profile than the larger, squarer American trucks.", "The appeal is in its familiar everyday shape: contemporary without looking exotic, substantial without adopting the visual bulk of a full-size luxury SUV. The Montagne fits naturally into a collection of modern American vehicles, especially if you like the cars that make the streets feel lived in. It has the right image for a weekend out of town or a perfectly ordinary afternoon. In GTA, an ordinary afternoon can be a fairly ambitious plan."],
  "vapid-riata-classic": ["The Vapid Riata ’70 takes its cues from the first-generation Ford Bronco, bringing a compact, upright utility-vehicle shape to GTA VI. Its simple panels and short-bodied proportions have a very different feel from the sprawling SUVs that followed.", "The appeal is in that uncomplicated silhouette. It looks right beside older pickups and classic American cars, with enough rugged visual character to suggest a day away from paved streets. The Riata ’70 is a vehicle for players who enjoy the shape and charm of early SUVs. A little weathering would feel more appropriate here than a velvet rope and a reservation."],
  "vapid-slamvan": ["The Vapid Slamvan ’56 brings hot-rod pickup style to GTA VI, drawing on the 1953–1956 Ford F-Series. Its rounded cab and old-fashioned truck proportions give it a very different presence from the tall, sharply styled pickups in the modern lineup.", "Two seats and rear-wheel drive complete the familiar layout. The Slamvan’s character is rooted in custom-car culture, where an old working shape becomes something worth standing around and studying. It suits a collection of classics, lowriders and unusual American metal. There’s a certain charm to a truck that looks like its owner went out for spare parts and came back with an entire hobby."],
  "vapid-stanier": ["Few sedan silhouettes in GTA VI are as familiar as that of the Vapid Stanier ’98. Its design takes cues from the Ford Crown Victoria. Its long body, upright cabin and conventional three-box shape are instantly familiar, even without a roof sign or a set of flashing lights.", "Four seats and rear-wheel drive keep the traditional American layout. This is the civilian Stanier, with its own appeal as a straightforward, recognizable road car. It looks natural outside a diner or parked among older sedans, and it adds something grounded to a collection of more dramatic machinery. Few silhouettes say ordinary traffic so clearly, even when the owner’s plans for the day are anything but ordinary."],
  "vapid-stanier-55": ["The Vapid Stanier ’55 captures a more decorative era of American car design in GTA VI, with Ford Fairlane Club Sedan influences. Its rounded body, decorative trim and upright cabin give it the character of a classic built when even everyday cars were allowed a little ceremony.", "The shape has a natural place against the city’s older architecture, especially on an evening when the light catches the chrome. It suits players who enjoy the history written into a car’s proportions rather than a long list of performance figures. The Stanier ’55 looks like it belongs in a holiday photograph, preferably one taken before anyone started checking the time."],
  "vulcar-ingot": ["The Vulcar Ingot has the long roof and practical proportions of an older station wagon in GTA VI, blending Volkswagen Passat wagon and Nissan Stagea influences. The straight roof and practical-looking rear body give it a familiar everyday character.", "Four seats and front-wheel drive sit beneath the unassuming exterior. The Ingot suits players who appreciate the quieter corners of a vehicle lineup, where ordinary family cars can be just as interesting as the obvious garage centerpieces. It looks like it should be carrying a shopping list, a folded road map and a very specific opinion about fuel prices. Sometimes that is exactly the kind of personality a collection needs."],
  "canis-kamacho": ["The Canis Kamacho brings military-inspired utility-truck attitude to GTA VI. Its design draws from the Jeep Crew Chief 715 and Nukizer 715 concepts, both rooted in the Kaiser Jeep M715. The tall stance, square cabin and open bed make it look like a modern pickup that reported for field duty.", "Four seats and all-wheel drive give the Kamacho room for the crew behind its rugged bodywork. It fits mud trails, remote roads and garages where a spotless finish is never the main objective. Some off-road trucks arrive with an adventure campaign. This Canis looks like it packed the tools and left before the meeting started."],
  "vapid-dominator-67-buggy": ["The Vapid Dominator ’67 Buggy turns the shape of a first-generation Ford Mustang into an off-road machine for GTA VI. Its familiar long hood and classic coupe body sit high on oversized tires, while protective hardware and roof lights shift the mood from boulevard to backwoods.", "This Ultimate Edition Vapid is for drivers who want vintage American lines without staying between the curbs. The raised stance and stripped-back buggy attitude give the old muscle-car silhouette a different purpose, somewhere between a trail build and a very confident refusal to take the paved route. Concours points were clearly not part of the brief."],
  // Launch texts (Codex Launch-Ueberarbeitung 21.11., Chavos XS 2nd paragraph Claude), approved by Fausto 21.11.2026
  "benefactor-schafter-s": ["The Schafter S brings Mercedes-Benz C-Class W205 styling to Benefactor’s sedans. Its appeal is the smaller executive-car idea: enough formality for a hotel entrance, with proportions that leave the limousine business to someone else.", "Beside the Schafter V12, it gives the familiar name a different character. There’s a whole corner of German car culture built around the everyday executive sedan, and the S belongs in that conversation without needing a stretched body or a motorcade."],
  "bf-greta": ["The BF Greta brings Volkswagen Jetta influence to Leonida’s everyday traffic. It puts the badge on a conventional sedan, with the sort of ordinary-road-car identity that can be easy to overlook among GTA’s more eccentric designs.", "That Jetta connection gives it a place in the German-car scene all its own. There’s an appeal to pulling into a meet in something that could just as easily be parked outside work, especially when everyone else has brought their weekend car."],
  // PLACEHOLDER (Claude 27.11.2026, own data only). Final text: Codex, outputs/CODEX-AUFTRAG-Fahrzeugtexte-Injection-73-Sandking-XT-2026-11-27.md
  "bf-injection-73": ["The BF Injection ’73 is a two-seat off-road car in GTA VI, inspired by the Volkswagen Beetle in Baja Bug form. Its upgrades go through the Off-Road specialist.", "Its in-game stats and ratings are added to this page as they are recorded."],
  "bravado-bogan": ["Bravado’s Bogan draws on the second-generation Chrysler Sebring and Dodge Stratus, bringing a very different piece of American sedan history into GTA VI. Those early-2000s references give it a more everyday identity than the Buffalo’s muscle-car styling.", "Put the two beside each other and the contrast tells the story: the familiar commuter and the sedan dressed to make an entrance. The Bogan belongs to the part of Bravado’s world that filled ordinary parking lots. That is part of American car culture, too."],
  "declasse-akane": ["Chevrolet Sonic influence gives the Declasse Akane a small-car starting point. It brings the everyday end of Chevrolet-inspired design into GTA VI, alongside the big American shapes more often associated with the Declasse badge.", "The family resemblance is more interesting for the difference in scale. An Akane and a Granger tell very different stories about the same fictional manufacturer, from a trip across town to a vehicle that takes up much more of the street."],
  "declasse-picador-72": ["A Picador has a foot in two different garages: classic car up front, pickup bed behind. The Declasse Picador ’72 carries the Chevrolet El Camino’s coupe-utility idea into GTA VI, with room for a passenger and an open cargo tray behind the cabin.", "The name has history, too. Picadors appeared in San Andreas, GTA V, and GTA Online, so the year on this one doesn’t make it a stranger to the series. It’s an easy fit beside classic muscle when you want the same period flavor with somewhere to put the spare wheels."],
  "dinka-chavos-xs": ["The Dinka Chavos XS has a familiar past under a different name. GTA Online players met it as the Chavos V6 in Agents of Sabotage; in GTA VI, it returns as the XS, with tenth-generation Honda Accord influence in its design.", "At Gellhorn Raceway, a tuned Chavos XS rental with a race livery lines up for Keep It PG. The stock car comes without it, so the track version shows how far an everyday Japanese sedan can be taken."],
  "ubermacht-rebla-gts": ["BMW’s fourth-generation X5 is the design reference for the Übermacht Rebla GTS. The taller SUV shape brings a different set of proportions to a badge whose coupes are already familiar sights at GTA car meets.", "This exact name also has history in GTA Online, where the Rebla GTS arrived with The Diamond Casino Heist. In Leonida, it brings that recognizable face back alongside the smaller Übermachts. Park one near a Cypher and the shared badge covers two very different ideas of a BMW-inspired car."],
  "vapid-lowline": ["The Lowline takes Vapid’s American sedan story toward the 2013–2019 Ford Taurus. It offers a newer design reference than the Crown Victoria influence associated with the Stanier, giving the badge another generation of ordinary road car to work with.", "That is a useful difference when the cars are parked together: related manufacturer, different chapter of American traffic. A Lowline belongs in the same conversation as the family sedans and company cars people remember from everyday roads."],
  "willard-grouse-92": ["The Willard Grouse ’92 brings sixth-generation Buick Skylark influence to GTA VI. It catches the family-sedan side of early-1990s American design, giving that decade a face beyond the sports cars that usually get remembered first.", "There is something familiar about a period car with an ordinary job. The Grouse fits the school-run and supermarket side of the ’90s, which makes it a different kind of nostalgic choice. Somebody had to drive everyone home from those car meets."],
  "willard-lasso-90": ["A Buick Reatta Convertible is an unusual place to start a GTA car, and that is the Willard Lasso ’90’s attraction. The reference brings a two-seat American convertible into the mix, with a different character from the large cruisers and muscle cars around it.", "The small cabin matters here: this is the more personal side of American motoring, built around the driver and one passenger. A Lasso makes sense when the drive is the plan and nobody has invited the whole crew."],
  "willard-transient": ["Willard’s Transient takes its cues from the sixth-generation Buick Regal, bringing a more recent sedan design to a badge with plenty of American-car associations. It gives the manufacturer a different reference point from the older Skylark-inspired Grouse ’92.", "The interest is in that change of generation. A Grouse and a Transient share a badge, but they represent different periods of the everyday sedan. The Transient carries Willard’s story forward from the early-1990s car parked next to it."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Vorbilder-23 P1-P5 (21.11.), Claude edits 1-7, approved by Fausto 21.11.2026 (Riata: rewrite pending)
  "benefactor-schutzen": ["Benefactor gives the Schutzen the proportions of a concept car that escaped the display stand. Its inspiration is the Vision Mercedes-Maybach 6, with a long hood and a cabin set well behind the front wheels.", "The tall, narrow grille bars give you something to look at beyond the sheer length of the body. Put it alongside a Schafter and the family resemblance becomes a difference in attitude: one arrives for a meeting, the other expects the meeting to come outside."],
  "bravado-bison": ["The plain Bravado Bison is the familiar middle generation in a growing pickup family. Its fourth-generation Dodge Ram Quad Cab roots place it between the older Bison 900 ’95 and the newer Bison 1800.", "That distinction matters more than another suffix on the tailgate. The Bison carries the shape many GTA V players already know, so it is a natural anchor for a truck lineup that stretches across several generations of Bravado."],
  "bravado-bison-1800": ["Bravado’s Bison 1800 moves the family toward the fifth-generation Ram 1500. The large crew cab is central to its shape, carrying the pickup idea into a more recent generation than the plain Bison.", "It is the modern Ram-style cab that separates the 1800 from its older Bison relatives."],
  // Codex 25.11.2026, approved by Fausto 27.11.2026 (dual rear wheels confirmed; "long bed" removed: not verified)
  "bravado-bison-3800": ["Dual rear wheels give the Bison 3800 a very different presence from the plain Bison. Its Ram 3500 inspiration puts it in heavy-duty truck territory, with the sort of broad stance that makes an ordinary pickup look restrained.", "The bigger number doesn’t bring higher ratings. The 3800 costs more to register than the plain Bison, while its stock road and off-road ratings are lower. This is the Bison for someone drawn to the heavy-duty look, rather than a higher-rated version of the familiar truck."],
  "bravado-bison-900": ["The Bison 900 ’95 is the older face of Bravado’s pickup family, with a design linked to the second-generation Dodge Ram. It gives the Bison name a different starting point from the later trucks, rather than simply dressing up the familiar model.", "A lineup of Bisons makes more sense with the full badges in view. The 900 ’95, plain Bison, and Bison 1800 belong to different generations of the idea, so an older American-truck collection has a reason to make room for this one."],
  "bravado-gresley-xt": ["The Gresley XT gives Bravado’s American styling a taller canvas. Its third-generation Dodge Durango inspiration puts the emphasis on a substantial family-car body, with a very different presence from the brand’s low-slung performance cars.", "The Durango influence is a useful part of Bravado’s identity: American-car attitude expressed through a family vehicle. The Gresley XT carries that character in a larger, upright body, where the connection to the brand’s performance cars becomes a matter of styling."],
  "bravado-sojourn": ["Bravado does the school run, too. The Sojourn follows the fifth-generation Dodge Grand Caravan, trading the brand’s usual performance-car image for the familiar outline of an American family minivan.", "It also appears in taxi form, which feels entirely at home on a busy Vice City street. The same basic shape can belong outside a house or under a cab roof sign, giving the Sojourn a part in the city that has little to do with showing off."],
  "canis-crawler-82": ["A small cargo bed gives the Canis Crawler ’82 a different shape from the usual Jeep-inspired trail rig. The Jeep Scrambler CJ-8 is the reference here, extending the familiar compact body into something closer to a little pickup.", "That combination is the appeal: an old Canis with space behind the cab, rather than another tall family wagon. The Scrambler shape gives it character before you add anything else."],
  "declasse-bobcat-xl-84": ["A long bed and square-edged bodywork give the Declasse Bobcat XL ’84 its working-truck character. It has the proportions of an older American pickup, with much of its presence coming from the length behind the cab.", "The truck looks at home in a dusty camp scene, where the boxy body has as much to say as the paint. That older, angular silhouette is the Bobcat XL ’84’s contribution to a pickup gathering, with the long bed giving the side view much of its character."],
  "declasse-impaler-20": ["The Impaler ’20 carries an old Declasse name into a much more recent shape. Its reference is the tenth-generation Chevrolet Impala, a full-size four-door far removed from the older Impalers familiar to lowrider fans.", "That contrast is what makes the name interesting across generations. The ’20 shows the later, more restrained end of the family: a large everyday car whose connection to the classics is easier to appreciate when they are parked together."],
  "declasse-parkland-71": ["The Parkland ’71 looks back to the Buick Estate of 1971–1976, bringing the big American station-wagon tradition into Declasse’s range. It is a different expression of seventies car culture from the coupes that usually get the attention.", "Think family road trips rather than a strip of drag-racing pavement. That is the visual appeal of an old full-size wagon: the same broad American-car presence, drawn out into a shape associated with luggage, long vacations, and very full driveways."],
  "declasse-rancher-86": ["Tall, angular bodywork and thick tires give the Declasse Rancher ’86 its back-country look. The open pickup bed is an important part of this version’s shape, keeping it distinct from the enclosed Rancher XL familiar from GTA V.", "The square-body styling lends itself to a scene outside a lumber yard or beside an old workshop. A little dirt in the setting does more for that character than a polished showroom floor; the Rancher looks like it belongs somewhere with a job to do."],
  "dundreary-arcturus-93": ["Dundreary’s Arcturus ’93 belongs to the age when American luxury still made room for a personal coupe. The Lincoln Mark VIII is its design reference, putting it on a different branch of the family tree from the brand’s imposing old four-doors.", "The appeal is that particular early-nineties idea of a car built around its owner rather than a whole household. It gives Dundreary a more intimate kind of luxury, with a two-door body that makes a quiet change from the bigger shapes around it."],
  "karin-allander": ["Karin’s Allander takes its shape from the fifth-generation Toyota RAV4, bringing a familiar compact crossover into Leonida’s traffic. It represents the everyday side of Japanese car design: the sort of shape you notice more once you start looking past the exotics.", "That RAV4 connection gives the Allander a different kind of familiarity from Karin’s older enthusiast cars. Its character comes from a recognizable family-crossover shape, the sort of design that earns its place in a street scene through everyday use rather than rarity."],
  "obey-animus": ["A long roofline flowing into the rear gives the Obey Animus its identity. It follows the Audi A7 Sportback approach, keeping the shape of a low fastback while making room for four doors.", "That makes a different kind of statement from the shorter 8F Drafter. The Animus puts more of its character into the sweep of the whole body, a shape best appreciated from the side."],
  "pegassi-vitello": ["Open a scissor door and the Pegassi Vitello has already made its introduction. The Lamborghini Aventador provides the design reference, giving this Pegassi the theatrical entrance that goes with an exotic Italian shape.", "The Aventador influence and the upward-opening doors make the Vitello hard to overlook, especially after dark."],
  "sirius-sungrazer-61": ["The Sirius Sungrazer ’61 reaches back to the early Mercury Comet for its design. It brings a different chapter of American car styling into GTA VI, before the later shapes that usually dominate a muscle-car meet.", "Give it a little space beside the newer cars and the age difference becomes part of the display. The Sungrazer belongs in a conversation about early-sixties American design, rather than being treated as another version of the later Sirius models."],
  "vapid-dominator-65": ["The Dominator ’65 takes Vapid’s Mustang connection back to the first generation. This is the early pony-car idea behind the later Dominators, with the appeal of a familiar name in its original design era.", "The ’65 is a natural place to begin a tour of the Dominator family, before the later generations changed the shape and scale of Vapid’s American performance car."],
  "vapid-montagne-pickup": ["The Montagne Pickup keeps much of the family-vehicle shape and adds a short cargo bed behind the cab. The Ford Explorer Sport Trac is the reference, a useful explanation for why this Vapid looks different from a conventional long-bed truck.", "Its proportions tell the story: a substantial four-door cabin, then a modest stretch of open bed. That slightly unusual balance is what separates the Montagne Pickup from Vapid’s more traditional trucks."],
  "vapid-montagne-xl": ["The Montagne XL gives Vapid an older family-car shape, drawing on the second-generation Ford Explorer. The upright body belongs to the period when an everyday American utility vehicle still looked closely related to a truck.", "That makes the XL interesting on its own terms, rather than simply as the bigger-sounding Montagne. Its turn-of-the-century character is the attraction: the kind of vehicle that helps a street scene feel lived in, especially with newer designs passing alongside it."],
  "vapid-reclaimer": ["There is more to Vapid pickups than ever-larger F-Series shapes. The Reclaimer takes its cues from the 2019–2023 Ford Ranger T6, bringing a narrower, midsize-truck outline to the range.", "Its appeal is easy to miss if every truck photo is about height and oversized tires. Keep the Reclaimer simple and the Ranger proportions come through: a modern pickup with a more compact visual footprint than the big American workhorses."],
  // Codex 25.11.2026, adopted 27.11.2026
  "vapid-reclaimer-70": ["The Reclaimer ’70 looks like it still has a shift to finish. Broad mirrors and a simple cab give it the character of an older working truck, with sixth-generation Ford F-Series styling behind the shape. The wooden-sided farm version adds another layer of everyday utility.", "That makes a useful contrast with the modern, Ranger-inspired Reclaimer. The older truck sits below it in both stock ratings, so the shared name doesn’t mean similar performance. Its appeal lies in the work-truck details: less modern pickup polish, more farmyard character."],
  "vapid-sandking-xl": ["The Sandking XL is Vapid’s big-truck idea with little interest in understatement. Ford Super Duty styling is the foundation, giving it a broad body and a large bed that make its scale part of the attraction.", "The name will be familiar from GTA V, and it still makes sense in a gathering of American pickups. Next to the more compact Reclaimer, the Sandking XL supplies the opposite end of the picture: a truck whose size does much of the talking."],
  // PLACEHOLDER (Claude 27.11.2026, own data only). Final text: Codex, outputs/CODEX-AUFTRAG-Fahrzeugtexte-Injection-73-Sandking-XT-2026-11-27.md
  "vapid-sandking-xt": ["The Vapid Sandking XT is a six-seat pickup in GTA VI, inspired by the 2020 Ford F-450 Super Duty Limited. It has six storage slots, and its upgrades go through the Off-Road specialist.", "In stock form, it matches the Sandking XL in speed, acceleration and off-road handling, but costs more to register and rates slightly lower on the road."],
  "vapid-stanier-g2": ["You may know the Stanier G2 better with police equipment attached. This is the model that appeared as the Police Cruiser in GTA V and the Stanier LE in GTA Online, now wearing its civilian identity in GTA VI.", "Its Ford Crown Victoria roots give it a familiar full-size American shape. Away from the police fittings, the appeal is in seeing that body as an ordinary car again, with more room for its everyday character than a rear-view mirror usually allows."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtext-Riata 21.11. (last sentence cut), approved by Fausto 21.11.2026
  "vapid-riata": ["The Vapid Riata owes its design to a fan-created vision of a future Ford Bronco. That independent concept mixed early Bronco cues with the look of newer Ford trucks, turning an enthusiast’s wish list into a design of its own.", "The Riata first arrived in GTA Online with The Doomsday Heist in December 2017 and returns in GTA VI. Its inspiration gives it a particular place in GTA’s car culture: a fictional truck rooted in fans imagining the return of a real nameplate."],
  // Codex Fahrzeugtexte-Neu-und-Platzhalter 23.11.2026, Claude edits, approved by Fausto 23.11.2026
  "schyster-woodland-85": ["A roof rack and an upright wagon body give the Schyster Woodland ’85 the look of an American family vacation on wheels. Its design draws on the Chrysler LeBaron Town & Country, with squared-off proportions and a formal chrome grille that seems unusually dressed up for the job.", "It also comes with wood-effect side panels, leaning further into the family-wagon look. The plain-sided version keeps things simpler, with the long roof and formal nose doing the work. Either way, the Woodland brings a different kind of nostalgia to GTA VI: school runs, luggage, and a car kept long after the kids moved out."],
  "invetero-coquette-64": ["The Invetero Coquette ’64 looks back to the Chevrolet Corvette C2, bringing that classic American sports-car shape to GTA VI. The long hood and sharply drawn body give it a different character from the newer Coquettes: more vintage Sting Ray than modern supercar.", "GTA V and GTA Online players know this car as the Coquette Classic. It is the Coquette for a classic-car meet or a coastal drive, with the kind of shape that needs very little decoration."],
  "declasse-bobcat-500-55": ["The Declasse Bobcat 500 ’55 takes the Bobcat name into classic American pickup territory. This is a separate truck from the Bobcat XL ’84, with a much older design at its heart. The appeal is closer to a vintage work truck than a modern crew hauler.", "Its vehicle menu lists Hot Rods as the specialist, a fitting connection for an old pickup with a second life ahead of it. A restrained restoration and a louder custom build belong to the same truck culture, and the Bobcat 500 brings a pickup to a classic collection instead of another coupe."],
};
